<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Cua Spaces.app (com.trycua.spaces.macos), Developer ID with the hardened
  runtime (scripts/build-release.sh).

  - automation.apple-events: App Teleport reads browser sessions with
    osascript (cua-teleport providers). With no `cua daemon` running the
    app runs the cua runtime in its own process (Cua.auto), so the app is
    the responsible process for those Apple Events, and macOS refuses them
    (-1743) from a hardened app without this entitlement. Info.plist carries
    NSAppleEventsUsageDescription for the prompt.

  Nothing else is needed, and nothing else is granted:
  - No JIT or unsigned executable memory: no web view, no script engine.
  - Library validation stays on: the only library the app loads is
    Contents/Frameworks/libcua_sdk.dylib, signed by the same team.
  - No keychain-access-groups: the Keyvault protector is a login keychain
    item whose ACL trusts the calling binary's designated requirement (team
    YCK386LBJ7 plus the signing identifier), not an access group, so it
    needs no provisioning profile.
  - Accessibility, Screen Recording and Touch ID (LocalAuthentication) are
    TCC or policy prompts, not entitlements, outside the App Sandbox.
  - Networking needs no entitlement outside the App Sandbox.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
